WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:05.760
Are you recording?

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:10.540
The question of the moment is, how is the
tragic passing of Justice Scalia going to

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:12.950
affect the 2016 race?

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.830
And there are two possible ways of looking
at it, sort of the difference between "is"

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:18.240
and "ought".

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.150
It ought to have a profound effect on the
2016 race.

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:26.580
It ought to be disqualifying for certain candidates,
particularly people like Donald Trump, who

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.490
give no evidence that they take the Constitution
particularly seriously.

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:34.610
How it is affecting the 2016 race kind of
remains to be seen.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:40.110
It certainly helps Ted Cruz, who has got a
very good brand in constitutional issues,

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:41.350
knows the Supreme Court well.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:44.160
It helps Marco Rubio to a lesser extent.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.670
But what it does do for both sides is it heightens
the stakes.

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:52.970
Everybody recognizes now that the future of
the Supreme Court essentially depends upon

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.310
this next presidential election.

00:00:55.310 --> 00:01:01.100
It will almost surely create a much uglier
political environment because the fight on

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:05.970
Capitol Hill is going to be bleeding into
the presidential race, and vice versa.

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:09.719
So, what are your thoughts on Justice Scalia?

00:01:09.719 --> 00:01:12.840
Let us know in the Comments, and also let
us know if there are any other topics that

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.210
you'd like us to cover in 60 seconds.

